# CHANGES -- what the game tells players has changed (src/changes.c).
# Each entry: a line '@ <id> <yyyy-mm-dd>', its text, then a blank line.
# Newest first. Ids never change and are never reused: a character's
# view counts are kept by id. Write entries for players, not for staff.

@ 20261004a 2026-10-04
GAINLIST now shows every skill and spell your class and guild can learn,
ticked (+) when you have it and crossed (X) when you do not, with what to
GAIN for it, which trainer sells it, where they stand and the WALKTO that
takes you there. ABILITIES is the same command, and GAINLIST TRAINERS is
the old list of what each trainer sells.

@ 20261004b 2026-10-04
The Oracle knows what you are missing. PRAY and ask her what skills or
spells you have not learned, and she answers from the game itself, with
the trainer and the way to them.

@ 20261004c 2026-10-04
Gate, earth travel and portal reach the first creature or person of that
name you could actually get to: anyone not in a no-recall room or a jail,
not immortal, and no more than four levels above you. 2.kitten is the
second such kitten. Astral walk has no level limit and can leave a no-
recall room, but never enter one.

@ 20261004d 2026-10-04
Hyrule can be done in order now. Levels 1 and 2 stood behind river
crossings that needed the raft, which is Level 3's treasure, and Level 4's
island behind a ladder that is Level 4's own. There are stepping stones, a
ferry and a plank bridge there now. Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261004e 2026-10-04
Nothing in Hyrule attacks first any more, and its creatures are as tough
as the rest of the world's at the same level - no tougher, no softer. The
land around each dungeon is graded for that dungeon, and HELP HYRULE lists
the character levels each dungeon is built for and where it is.

@ 20261004f 2026-10-04
Every Hyrule guardian can drop a piece for every armour slot, each the
best in the game for its dungeon's levels, for fighters and casters alike,
and three fall each kill. The guardians' weapons and Heart Guards are
stronger too.

@ 20261004g 2026-10-04
In Hyrule, enemies killed near a cracked wall sometimes leave a bomb, so
you are not sent back to a shop to get past a wall the dungeon put in
front of you.

@ 20261004h 2026-10-04
The Recorder: PLAY RECORDER (or BLOW RECORDER) out in Hyrule's open land
calls a whirlwind that carries you to any dungeon you have won and to the
one you are working on. PLAY RECORDER <level> picks one. Where a puzzle
wants the tune, the puzzle still gets it.

@ 20261004i 2026-10-04
Leave a Hyrule dungeon you have won by its returning light and an owl
lands to tell you where the next dungeon is and what opens it. The Oracle
knows every path in Hyrule too, and gives directions from wherever you
stand.

@ 20261004j 2026-10-04
A Hyrule treasure chest is never relocked while you are standing at it.

@ 20261004k 2026-10-04
Mudlet 1.5.5: Hyrule's dungeons are no longer on the starter map. Pick up
a dungeon's map and the whole dungeon is drawn on yours.

@ 20261004l 2026-10-04
Commands typed on one line with semicolons between them - n;n;e - run one
after another in any client, as they always did in the browser client.

@ 20261004m 2026-10-04
The quest master tells you your quest instead of announcing it to the
room.

@ 20261004n 2026-10-04
A remort keeps your unspent practices and trains, and your own flaming
aura never burns you.

@ 20261004o 2026-10-04
Spells your class can learn from another class's trainer are taught now,
and so is DESPAIR. MAJOR GLOBE, the travel spells, riding, MAZE and WALKTO
had fixes of their own.

@ 20261004p 2026-10-04
The slot machines pay back about 93 percent, and limited items you put in
your stash stay yours.

@ 20261004q 2026-10-04
Mud School's north cage now warns you plainly: its monster attacks the
moment you walk in, so go in rested and FLEE if it turns against you.

@ 20261004r 2026-10-04
The play page has a link to the gear finder: the best gear for your class
and level, and where it drops.

@ 20261003a 2026-10-03
Psionic powers start at 1% until you practise them with Salir, including
powers handed back after a remort.

@ 20261003b 2026-10-03
Nobody can remort or level past the level cap, and every necromancer spell
now has a trainer. SCRIBE is taught by Dawn for every class.

@ 20261003c 2026-10-03
WALKTO <place> walks you to any area, guild hall, guildmaster or trainer
from wherever you stand, a step at a time. Type anything to stop. See HELP
WALKTO.

@ 20261003d 2026-10-03
The Oracle knows every guild hall, guildmaster and trainer, and the way to
each.

@ 20261003e 2026-10-03
Hyrule's nine dungeons are done in order: each guardian drops a key to its
treasure chest, which holds a Triforce piece and the treasure the next
dungeon needs. COMBINE TRIFORCE joins all nine. Ganon guards the Master
Sword and is a fight for a group. Dungeon maps and compasses show you the
way. See HELP HYRULE.

@ 20261003f 2026-10-03
Hyrule prices everything in ordinary gold.

@ 20261003g 2026-10-03
Stealth and shadowmeld cannot be seen through without holylight - there is
no roll any more, so you no longer flicker in and out of sight.

@ 20261003h 2026-10-03
REPAIR costs what your kills can pay for.

@ 20261003i 2026-10-03
Characters can have more than 32,767 hit points.

@ 20261003j 2026-10-03
Heroes never get too full to eat, and nobody sees 'No help on that word'
at login. Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261003k 2026-10-03
Every guild has infravision, titles stay set, and an ALIAS can run several
commands separated by semicolons.

@ 20261003l 2026-10-03
An item the game retires is swapped for its replacement at your next login
instead of vanishing.

@ 20261003m 2026-10-03
Mudlet 1.5.2 to 1.5.4: health, mana, endurance and experience are back
across the top, a failing part no longer hides the interface, death traps
are off the map, and travel routes load by default.

@ 20261002a 2026-10-02
COMPARE is rebuilt around how hard you hit, and COMPARE UPGRADES lists the
best pieces you could be wearing. The website's gear finder follows the
same rules.

@ 20261002b 2026-10-02
PRAY takes you to the Oracle's sanctum and back.

@ 20261002c 2026-10-02
Old bug and typo reports that were still true have been fixed, and the
disarm message has lost its stray space.

@ 20261001a 2026-10-01
The Oracle: PRAY to ask a seer about the game - gear, places, levelling,
how things work. See HELP ORACLE.

@ 20261001b 2026-10-01
A remort keeps every piece of your gear, bagging what your new level
cannot wear, and REPLAY is another name for HISTORY.

@ 20261001c 2026-10-01
SWEDISH works again.  The command set a flag but nothing read it: the
speech filter that garbles a swedished (or drunk) player's SAY and
channel text had been dropped in a refactor and left only as an
uncompiled file.  It is compiled and wired back into SAY and the
channels.  Drunk slurring returns with it.

@ 20261001d 2026-10-01
Mudlet 1.5.0 adds a combat-awareness set: a lag bar that shows when
you can act again, an enemy health gauge beside your own bars, a
Buffs tab with a countdown bar per spell, a Group tab showing each
party member's level and health, a low-health warning, and a Tells
tab that lights up on a new tell.  Update the package to get them.

@ 20261001e 2026-10-01
Mudlet: the quest strip now carries the target room, and clicking it
(or typing WALK QUEST) walks you straight there. The game sends the
room's vnum with the quest, so it is an exact path, not a guess by
name. Update the package to 1.4.0 to get it.

@ 20261001f 2026-10-01
The dashboard's gear finder names the best piece for each of your
eighteen slots for your class and level - both rings, both necks and
both wrists, two different items for each pair - then ranks every
item you could wear in each slot, Light included.  Plain
armour and shields were missing because their own armour class was
never counted, lights because they carry no wear flag, and an item
that made your saves worse was being ranked as if it made them
better.

@ 20261001g 2026-10-01
Staff can eat anything again, to destroy an item they carry.  It
checked the character's level rather than their trust, so a builder
trusted to immortal rank was told the item was not edible.

@ 20261001h 2026-10-01
The training dummy can no longer be finished off.  A fatality
backstab killed it outright, because an instant kill never passed
the check that keeps it standing.  Backstab it and you get an
ordinary backstab, counted on the meter like any other blow; and
anything else that kills on the spot now finds it back on its post.

@ 20261001i 2026-10-01
AFFECT now lists psionic wards.  MINDBAR, PSIONIC ARMOR and PSYCHIC
SHIELD change no statistic - they are a named protection and a
duration - and the list was skipping exactly that shape, so the one
kind of effect you most want to confirm was the one you could not
see.  Reported by Alaric.  Psionics and skills are also no longer
announced as spells.

@ 20261001j 2026-10-01
Damage numbers now appear for every weapon.  Fifteen weapons in the
world carry no particular attack noun, and those went down a branch
of the combat message code that had never been given the bracketed
figure - so DAMAGENUMBERS worked for every weapon except the odd
ones, and for bare hands in some cases.  Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261001k 2026-10-01
A training yard, and a dummy in it that cannot be killed.  Go down
the staircase in the centre of the Oak Tree Square, then south -
WALK DUMMY in Mudlet takes you there - and KILL DUMMY.  HELP DUMMY
explains all of it.  The yard takes one fighter at a time, so nobody
else can walk into your run.

@ 20261001l 2026-10-01
Every run is the standard fight by default: twenty-five rounds, then a
bell, against a dummy at your own level that fights normally - it
dodges, parries, blocks and hits back.  Your best goes on a
leaderboard - DUMMY LEADERBOARD - and when a run ends you are told
whether it was a personal best, where you stand among everybody who
has run it, and how far the record is.  Post the best run anybody has
and you earn Top of the Board.

@ 20261001m 2026-10-01
Just attacking the dummy gives you the standard fight: when the yard
empties, it goes back to it, whatever the last fighter set.

@ 20261001n 2026-10-01
Only the standard fight is ranked.  DUMMY DEFENDS NO and DUMMY FIGHTS
NO take the dummy's own part out so you can measure your damage
alone, and DUMMY ROUNDS and DUMMY ENDLESS change the length - but
changing any setting at all means the run is not ranked, and the game
says so the moment you change it.

@ 20261001o 2026-10-01
Neither of you can die in the yard.  When a run ends you are put back
the way you were when it began - hit points, mana and moves - not
healed to full, so it is no place to recover.  Nothing is learned
there either: skills and spells do not improve in the yard.

@ 20261001p 2026-10-01
The report breaks the fight down attack by attack, both ways - every
spell you cast and every special attack on its own line, with its
damage, share, hit rate, average and best - alongside your totals,
damage per second, per swing and per round, and everything it did
to you.  Set the dummy up however the question needs: any level,
four shapes, nine damage types, a spell for it to cast, haste, a
different number of rounds, or DUMMY ENDLESS for a run with no
bell.

@ 20261001q 2026-10-01
A portal now refuses to take you into a private room that is full,
the way walking in always has.  It used to be the one way past.

@ 20261001r 2026-10-01
The quest master no longer asks you to kill the training dummy, which
cannot die.

@ 20261001s 2026-10-01
Mudlet shows your damage per round under the target: live during a
fight, then the last fight's once it ends.  Every fight counts, and
the game measures it, so it works with damage numbers off.  A new
line below the quest lists who else is online - only players you
could see, so nobody wizi, cloaked, stealthed or hidden.  Mudlet
offers the 1.3.0 package update automatically.

@ 20261001t 2026-10-01
City guards hunting a wanted player no longer follow them into the
Temple.  A hunter stops at the edge of a room mobiles may not enter,
as it always has at a safe one.

@ 20261001u 2026-10-01
If WALK DUMMY in Mudlet still heads somewhere else, TOCGUI ATLAS
reloads the map with the yard where it is now.

@ 20261001v 2026-10-01
The Mudlet chat window now shows each channel in the colour you
chose for it with COLOR, the same as the main window, and the quest
strip says where the quest master last saw your target.  Mudlet
offers the 1.3.1 package update automatically.

@ 20261001w 2026-10-01
The plaque in the Hall of Heroes lists every hero there has ever
been, and a new hero's name is on it the moment they are made - as
the room always said it would be.  LOOK PLAQUE, down from the
centre of the Oak Tree Square.

@ 20261001x 2026-10-01
POKE pokes again.  It was taken as the start of the longer command
POKER, so the social could never be used.  A word that is exactly a
social's name is now that social.

@ 20261001y 2026-10-01
COMBINE is back.  It switches your inventory between the combined
list - (3) a big pot pie - and the long one, and AUTOLIST shows which
you have.  It had been switched off while everything it controls
stayed on.  COMB is still the social, so type at least COMBI.

@ 20261001z 2026-10-01
Pyrotechnics now hits as hard as a fireball cast at your level.  It
used to scale with your current hit points, which made it about three
times its fellow psionics at level fifty and grew without limit with
every remort.  A failed attempt now costs its wait, as a failed cast
does, rather than letting you try again at once.  Heating the
victim's gear is still what it adds over a fireball.

@ 20260925a 2026-09-25
RECALL can be moved.  RECALL SET makes the room you are standing in your
recall point, RECALL DEFAULT puts it back to the Temple, and RECALL WHERE
tells you where it is.  Once every 30 minutes, and not mid-fight.

@ 20260925b 2026-09-25
The note board answers back.  NOTE REPLY <n> starts a note to
whoever wrote that one with the subject already set, NOTE FORWARD
<n> <player> passes one on, NOTE SEARCH finds a note by any word in
it, NOTE UNREAD shows only what is waiting and NOTE CATCHUP clears
the lot.  See HELP NOTE.

@ 20260925c 2026-09-25
HISTORY draws a line where you last logged out, so what was said
while you were away is easy to pick out.  Nothing is shown to you
automatically - you have to ask.

@ 20260925d 2026-09-25
HISTORY reads back what was said.  Type it on its own for the last
twenty lines across every channel you can hear, HISTORY 50 for more,
HISTORY GOSSIP for one channel, or HISTORY TELL for your own tells -
which stay private, and are kept per character.  It is held in memory
and is lost on a reboot, so it is a way to catch up rather than a
transcript.  See HELP HISTORY.

@ 20260925e 2026-09-25
You can set your recall point at the quest giver now.  A room was
being refused for being 'private', which is a count of who is standing
in it - the questmaster and you already made two - and that count
changes minute to minute, so a point set in a quiet moment would have
quietly reverted to the Temple later.  Only the permanent flags refuse
a recall point now.

@ 20260925f 2026-09-25
A mobile that lives in a room no longer fills it either.  The quest
giver's room holds two, and the questmaster was one of them.

@ 20260925g 2026-09-25
An idle immortal no longer fills a one-person room.  Standing in the
quest room was enough to shut questing down for everybody else, which
is not what that flag is for - it exists to stop players walking in on
each other.  Staff can also walk into such a room now rather than
being turned away from it.

@ 20260925h 2026-09-25
STASH LINK has a help entry of its own at last: HELP STASHLINK covers
linking, denying, blocking and sharing in full, and HELP STASH lists
every subcommand rather than four of them.

@ 20260925i 2026-09-25
SHADOWMELD is a real skill now, and it is meant for two things: going
AFK without being killed for it, and laying in wait in a room somebody
has to walk through so that you strike first.

@ 20260925j 2026-09-25
The fourth remort teaches it at 50% and it improves from there with
use and with failure, like anything else.  A god can grant it to
anyone with SET SKILL.  No later remort takes it away, and once you
hold it you may practise it up.

@ 20260925k 2026-09-25
It behaves exactly like STEALTH against other players now rather than
like hide - the same roll against the same weather - so looking for
the hidden no longer finds you.  Holylight still does, and faerie fog
still reveals you.  VIS steps you out of it, WHO shows [SHADOW] beside
your name, WHERE leaves you off the list and DANGER SENSE counts you,
all exactly as they do for stealth.  Striking at somebody ends it,
whether you swing or cast.

@ 20260925l 2026-09-25
The recall that never fails has moved from the fourth remort down to
the third, to make room for shadowmeld.

@ 20260925m 2026-09-25
Remorting no longer cares which guilds you have belonged to, only
which classes you have lived as: mage, cleric, thief, warrior, monk,
necro.  Every life must be a class you have not played.  Join any
guild you like, as often as you like.

@ 20260925n 2026-09-25
The third remort now carries three gifts instead of one: twice the
carrying room, twice as long before the idle void, and a second psionic
power from each discipline.  Psionics STACK from now on -- a remort
remembers what it gave you and hands it back, so a later life never
costs you a power you already had, and the fifth remort gives you all
seventeen.

@ 20260925o 2026-09-25
Remorting no longer reads your class and guild history as one list.  It
used to, and because a guild is stored as its matching class, having
been in the mage guild barred you from ever living as a mage.  Worse, a
player who spent their choices badly could arrive at the fourth remort
with nothing legal left to pick, stuck at 57 with 59 out of reach.  The
two histories are separate now, 'none' is always a legal guild, and a
refusal lists everything still open to you.

@ 20260925p 2026-09-25
Two new gifts for remorting.  The remort taken at level 56 doubles
how long you may idle before the void takes you.  The one taken at
level 57 gives SHADOWMELD: draw the shadows around yourself and stay
in them until you move, sleeping if you like, with no creature in the
world able to see you.  It is meant for stepping away from the
keyboard.  See HELP SHADOWMELD.

@ 20260925q 2026-09-25
There is a stash at the altar now, one step west of recall.  STASH
PUT sets something aside from anywhere in the world; STASH GET takes
it back out, and that part only works at the altar.  Fifty things to
begin with, more for coin.  See HELP STASH.

@ 20260925r 2026-09-25
Hermie answers HEAL now, exactly like the healer at the pit and
with the same menu, except that everything she does is free.  She
no longer listens to what you say in the room.  She has ten more
spells than she did, six named groups, and REFRESH, HEAL and MANA
now fill the pool instead of handing out a slice at a time.  See
HELP BUFF.

@ 20260925s 2026-09-25
The healer at the pit tells you when a curse resists instead of
taking your gold in silence.

@ 20260925t 2026-09-25
The game says when something is waiting for you.  Unread notes are
announced at login instead of sitting unmentioned, and staff are told
how many bug, typo and idea reports have come in since they last
looked.  See HELP REPORTS.

@ 20260925u 2026-09-25
Staff can now MIRROR a player's gear onto themselves to look at a
build from the inside, online or not, and INVULN stops anything hurting
them while they do it.  MIRROR RESTORE hands the borrowed kit back in a
pack and puts their own gear on again.

@ 20260925v 2026-09-25
Herbs and spell components actually appear now.  They had barely been
landing at all for years, and the scattering is deliberately sparse -
finding one should be a small event - and stops entirely when nobody is
logged in.

@ 20260925w 2026-09-25
Two monster wards that had never worked now do.  A bloody aura turns
magic aside; a dominion shield turns aside everything, and only goes up
when the creature is badly hurt.  Four end-game creatures use them: the
Lord General and the Fade in the Battleground, and Zoltan and the second
succubus in Valhalla.  See HELP DOMINION SHIELD.

@ 20260925x 2026-09-25
WORD OF RECALL is worth casting now.  It always goes to the Temple
whatever you have set your own recall to, so a cleric has two places to
reach in a hurry instead of one, and it works while you are cursed,
where the RECALL skill does not.  A scroll or potion of recall carries
the same spell and does the same two things.

@ 20260925y 2026-09-25
Shops take the coins you actually have.  Buying used to look only at the
loose copper in your purse, so a character carrying platinum could be
told they could not afford a loaf of bread.  Shops now make change, and
they pay for what you sell them in coins you can carry.

@ 20260925z 2026-09-25
Prices in low-level areas are priced for low-level characters.  Mud
School sells bread for a copper and a meal for sixteen; a full set of
leather in Dresden is a few gold rather than a few platinum.  Nothing
above level 10 changed.

@ 20260924a 2026-09-24
AQUEST INFO, POINTS, TIME and GAMBLE work wherever you are standing;
only the questmaster's business needs a questmaster.  Every subcommand
can be shortened to its first letter.  Characters under level 4 can be
given a quest at last, and the questmaster now names an area you would
recognise instead of reading out its level range.

@ 20260924b 2026-09-24
REMORT no longer quietly costs you armour.  Gear you keep on through a
remort keeps its bonuses.  Remorting also works if your password has a
capital letter in it, which it did not before.

@ 20260924c 2026-09-24
REPAIR works on gear you are wearing, quotes its price in coins, and
restores an item's armour and worth as well as its condition.

@ 20260924d 2026-09-24
Travel directions to every area in the game are published on the website
at toc.jeremybean.com, and in the Routes panel of the browser client.

@ 20260924e 2026-09-24
Hyrule lets you recall out of it, except from inside the nine dungeons,
and its overworld no longer goes pitch dark at sunset.

@ 20260915a 2026-09-15
Prices are counted in copper.  LIST and APPRAISE write them in the coins
they will cost you - 5g 20s, 1c, free - instead of one long number.

@ 20260915b 2026-09-15
The necromancer's undead line works: CREATE SKELETON, CREATE ZOMBIE and
the rest.  ANIMATE PARTS no longer needs a body part, and hits harder
when it has one.

@ 20260915c 2026-09-15
CAST no longer needs quotes around a spell with a space in its name.

@ 20260915d 2026-09-15
Rooms built in game survive a reboot.
